# ---------- Agent / tooling artefacts ----------
# Playwright MCP scratch output
.playwright-mcp/
# Generated by `next dev` in every app; regenerated on each run
apps/*/AGENTS.md
apps/*/CLAUDE.md

# Design handoff bundles — a designer's raw export directory, ignored because it is a
# delivery mechanism rather than source: it arrives with a new name each time and carries
# screenshots, thumbnails and two READMEs that say which file happened to be open.
#
# The DESIGN ITSELF IS COMMITTED, in docs/design/source/ — all fourteen .dc.html files plus
# their three runtime scripts. That is what apps/web/src/app/design-coverage.test.ts reads and
# what every fidelity test compares against, so the "1:1 with the design" claim is checked on
# every push instead of skipping wherever the export was not checked out.
#
# It used to be the other way round: two superseded v1.0 files in docs/design/source and the
# current fourteen ignored. Screens then got built from whichever copy their author opened —
# one listing nineteen sidebar modules, the other twenty-four — which is exactly how one
# product ended up with two designs in it.
#
# Refreshing the design means dropping a new export beside the repo and copying its
# project/*.dc.html over docs/design/source/. The test prefers the export when it is present.
Restaurant form scope questions-handoff*/

# Expo CLI state — per machine, like .next/cache
.expo/
expo-env.d.ts

# Playwright output
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
